KAFE LEMBARAN: VIDEO CREATING METHOD
=====================================
Reference file for making every channel video. Read this first, follow it step by step,
and add to the CHANGE LOG at the bottom whenever the method changes.
Series name: "DUA HIRUPAN KOPI". Channel: @kafe.lembaran (TikTok, YouTube Shorts, Instagram Reels).
Pilot episode: "Kejatuhan Jensen Huang" (book: Adikuasa, Ayman Rashdan Wong), 16 Nov 2026.
Companion file: docs/video-style.txt (colours, fonts, references, older decisions).


0. THE FORMAT IN ONE GLANCE
---------------------------
  9:16 vertical, 1080x1920, 30 fps, about 60-80 s (follows the voiceover length).

  [0.0 s]  SOUND: kopitiam call "Bang, order bang!"
  [~1.3 s] SOUND A: "ahh" (satisfied sip)
  [OPENING, ~8 s]   Title card: "DUA HIRUPAN KOPI" tag, 2-line title, coffee cup with steam,
                    narrator line appears in sync with the voice:
                    "Biar saya terangkan isu ini... di antara dua hirupan kopi."
  [MIDDLE, ~65 s]   10-12 scenes, one per sentence of the voiceover. Stopwatch counts up at
                    the top ("Antara dua hirupan kopi"). Each scene = headline + visual panel
                    + full-sentence subtitle above the banner.
  [CLOSING, ~5-8 s] Stopwatch freezes in gold. Cup drops onto the saucer -> SOUND B: "ting".
                    Channel info + book pop in: Kafe Lembaran / BUKU DALAM VIDEO INI / TITLE /
                    Author / gold button "LINK BUKU KAT BIO" / kafelembaran.com / @kafe.lembaran.
                    Voice: "Nak faham permainan ni? Baca <buku>. Link kat bio."
  Under everything: kopitiam chatter (low), soft tick every second while the stopwatch runs.
  Bottom: Kafe Lembaran banner (always visible, bottom 256 px).


1. STEP-BY-STEP WORKFLOW (per episode)
--------------------------------------
  1. Pick the news story + the book it links to. Check the Shopee affiliate link exists.
  2. Research with sources (web search). Write down each fact with its source.
     Legal rules (section 8) apply to every line.
  3. Write the script (Malay, 12-14 short sentences, ~150-180 words) using the template
     in section 3. Each sentence = one scene.
  4. Voiceover in Google AI Studio (section 4). Download the .wav.
  5. Footage: generate 3-5 Gemini/Veo clips for the scenes that need real-looking images
     (section 5). Other scenes use animated infographic panels (section 6).
  6. Claude measures the pauses in the voiceover (ffmpeg silencedetect), maps each sentence
     to its start time, and sets SCN_T (scene starts), SUBS (subtitle starts) and OUT_T
     (closing start) in the render script. Rule: scene starts 0.3 s before its sentence.
  7. Render (section 7). Check a contact sheet of frames + listen to the audio.
  8. User reviews on phone -> feedback -> re-render.
  9. Upload the .mp4 to the repo media/ folder (served by GitHub Pages) and schedule with
     Metricool: TikTok + YouTube Shorts (+ Instagram). Switch ON the AI-generated label.


2. LAYOUT (pixels on the 1080x1920 frame)
-----------------------------------------
  y  96   Stopwatch, Share Tech Mono 64, white (gold when frozen). Format MM:SS:CC.
  y 185   "Antara dua hirupan kopi", Inter Bold 34, cream 80%.
  y 330-650  Headline: big number/word in Lora Bold 170-230, gold (#f2c14e),
             with 1 short sub-line in Inter SemiBold 52, cream.
             Kinds: big (fade/slide up), type (typewriter year), count (count-up number),
             stamp (orange DAKWAAN stamp that slams in with a shake).
  y 790-1330 VISUAL PANEL 960x540 at x=60: rounded 28 px, thin gold border.
             Footage (slow push-in) or animated infographic. Fades/slides in over 0.45 s.
  y 1342  "Sumber: ..." Inter 28, cream 60%, right-aligned (only for news/claims).
  y ~1457-1625 SUBTITLE: the full sentence the voice is saying, Poppins Bold 60,
             white with thick black outline, max width 960, wraps to 2-3 lines, sits just
             above the banner. Keywords in gold by wrapping in *stars* (e.g. *didakwa*).
  y 1664-1920 Banner (banner.png): cream band, cup logo, "Kafe Lembaran",
             kafelembaran.com · @kafe.lembaran.
  Scene change: 0.3 s cross-fade. Theme: "Kafe Klasik" (sample 1) =
  backgrounds alternate #165450 / #123f3c, text cream #f7f1e8, accent gold #f2c14e,
  alert orange #e07a3a.


3. SCRIPT TEMPLATE
------------------
  Opening line (fixed): "Biar saya terangkan isu ini... di antara dua hirupan kopi."
  Arc: who -> background -> what they built (one TECHNICAL fact explained simply) ->
       how big -> the event (dates) -> allegation (with "didakwa", plus the denial) ->
       outcome -> why it matters (geopolitics) -> MALAYSIA angle -> "kita di tengah".
  Closing line (fixed pattern): "Nak faham permainan ni? Baca <Buku>. Link kat bio."
  Write numbers as words where the voice must say them right
  ("sembilan puluh peratus", "dua belas November"); subtitles show digits.
  Use "..." where you want a pause.

  Pilot script (Jensen Huang):
    Biar saya terangkan isu ini... di antara dua hirupan kopi.
    Jensen Huang. Pengasas Nvidia, tahun 1993.
    Lahir di Taiwan, tahun 1963.
    Nvidia buat cip GPU... cip yang boleh buat ribuan kiraan serentak. Itulah enjin di sebalik AI.
    Hari ini, Nvidia kuasai hampir sembilan puluh peratus pasaran cip AI dunia.
    Tapi pada lapan November, lembaga Nvidia buka siasatan.
    Huang didakwa rapat dengan seorang wanita yang disyaki perisik China. China dan syarikat wanita itu menafikan.
    Empat hari kemudian, dua belas November... Huang letak jawatan. Tiga puluh tiga tahun sebagai CEO, berakhir.
    Kenapa ini penting? Sebab cip AI ialah minyak abad ke-21.
    Sejak 2022, Amerika sekat eksport cip AI canggih ke China.
    Dan Malaysia? Kita kendalikan tiga belas peratus pemasangan dan ujian cip dunia.
    Bila gergasi bergaduh... kita di tengah.
    Nak faham permainan ni? Baca Adikuasa. Link kat bio.
  Sources used: Nvidia 8-K (SEC), Al Jazeera, NBC, CBS, AP / AI Business, Fortune (~90%),
  MIDA (13%).


4. VOICEOVER: GOOGLE AI STUDIO (free tier)
------------------------------------------
  aistudio.google.com -> Playground -> model picker -> "Gemini 3.8 Flash TTS".
  Click the "The Master Storyteller" card to open the speech editor.
  Speaker: "Speaker 1 - Enzo", style "Friendly"   <- CHOSEN VOICE (16 Nov 2026)
  Paste the script, Run, then the download icon (bottom bar) -> .wav (24 kHz mono).
  Pilot result: 75.5 s.
  Notes:
   - "Create new voice" (Voice Design) needs a PAID API key: do not use.
   - Google Vids AI voiceover does NOT support Malay. CapCut TTS has Malay (backup option).
   - Test the first line before running the whole script; listen for numbers and
     Indonesian-sounding accent.
   - If the read is too fast, use "+ Expression": "slow, calm pace, relaxed pauses",
     or Claude can slow it 10-20% (ffmpeg atempo, pitch unchanged).


5. FOOTAGE AND SOUNDS FROM GEMINI (Veo video)
---------------------------------------------
  Clips are ~8-10 s, come out landscape 16:9 (fits the 960x540 panel perfectly).
  Rules in every prompt: no faces of real people (silhouettes / backs / blurred),
  no text, no logos, "No music". Gemini adds a small sparkle watermark: keep it
  (it is part of the AI disclosure).
  Scene prompts used in the pilot:
   - Taiwan 1963: "Vertical video, vintage 1960s film look, grainy, sepia tones. A quiet street
     in old Taipei, Taiwan, with low shophouses and bicycles. A family seen only as dark
     silhouettes from behind, walking away from the camera. Slow push-in. Soft ambient street
     sound, no music, no speech, no text, no faces."
   - Chip: "Vertical video, macro shot. A silicon wafer and a computer graphics chip under
     dramatic cool lighting, tiny reflections sweeping across the circuits, slow rotation.
     Clean, technical, high detail. Soft electronic hum, no music, no speech, no text, no logos."
   - Servers: "Vertical video. A long corridor of data-centre server racks glowing with green
     and blue lights, camera gliding slowly forward, lights pulsing like data flowing. Cool,
     powerful mood. Low machine hum, no music, no speech, no text, no logos."
   - Meeting room: "Vertical video, moody and tense. A dim, closed meeting room seen through
     frosted glass. Several businessmen appear only as blurred dark silhouettes around a
     table, no faces visible. A desk lamp flickers slightly. Slow, steady camera. Quiet room
     tone, no music, no speech, no text."
  Sound prompts:
   - Kopitiam call (gives "Bang, order bang!" at ~2.7-3.5 s of the clip): "Static shot inside
     a busy traditional Malaysian kopitiam in the morning, marble tables, ceiling fans,
     customers blurred in the background. A man off-camera calls out loudly and casually to
     the waiter in Malay: "Bang, order bang!" Then natural kopitiam ambience: people chatting
     softly in the background, no clear words, cups clinking. No music."
   - Chatter bed: "Static wide shot of a crowded traditional Malaysian kopitiam at breakfast
     time, every table full, ceiling fans spinning, customers blurred in the background.
     Sound: lively, busy chatter from many people talking at once at nearby tables, mixed
     Malay, Chinese and English voices overlapping so no single word is clear, occasional
     laughter, cups and spoons clinking. Steady and continuous. No music, no one speaking
     directly to the camera."  (+ the "Nearby tables" variant)
   - If Gemini adds music: add "Sound effects only. No background music, no spoken words."
   - Gemini refused a "barista close-up ... grinding" prompt; it also kept adding music to
     café prompts. Kopitiam prompts worked.


6. VISUAL PANELS (middle section)
---------------------------------
  Every scene MUST have a panel (feedback 16 Nov: "middle section too empty").
  Footage panel when a real-looking image helps (place, object, mood).
  Infographic panel when explaining an idea. Built-in infographics (video/cards.py):
    gpu       CPU (4 big cores lighting one by one) vs GPU (12x12 tiny cores all flashing)
    pair      two person icons + dotted line + "?" (allegation of a link)
    calendar  calendar page flips in (date) + "CEO" struck through + successor
    timeline  1993 -> 2026 bar filling, counting "33 tahun sebagai CEO"
    oil       oil barrel "=" chip ("Abad ke-20: minyak / Abad ke-21: cip AI")
    block     chip travels AMERIKA -> CHINA and is stopped by a red no-entry sign
    chain     chip supply chain: Reka bentuk > Fabrikasi wafer > Pemasangan & ujian (MALAYSIA)
    middle    AMERIKA and CHINA circles pushing in, small "MY" circle shaking between them
  Extra overlay on footage: progress bar (e.g. "NVIDIA ~90%" over the servers clip).
  Pilot mapping: 1 chip clip | 2 Taipei clip | 3 gpu | 4 servers + 90% bar | 5 meeting clip |
  6 pair | 7 calendar | 8 timeline | 9 oil | 10 block | 11 chain | 12 middle.


7. SOUND DESIGN AND MIX
-----------------------
  Fixed sounds (video/sfx/):
    shout.wav   "Bang, order bang!" (cut from the Gemini kopitiam clip 2.45-3.85 s)   at 0.0 s
    ahh_A.wav   sound A, satisfied "ahh" (from Gemini coffee clip, 5.8-6.8 s)          at ~1.25 s
    ting_B.wav  sound B, cup on saucer (from Gemini coffee clip, 8.5-9.2 s; peak 0.143 s
                into the file) -> placed so the peak lands when the cup touches the saucer
  Voice starts at OFF = 2.6 s (after the call and the "ahh").
  Chatter bed: two Gemini chatter clips (0.3-9.9 s each), chained with 1.2 s cross-fades in
    two layers (second layer starts 4.7 s in, left/right swapped) so the loop is not heard.
    Level 0.85 before the voice starts, 0.32 under the voice (smoothed 0.3 s).
  Tick: 1800 Hz click, 30 ms, every second while the stopwatch runs (quiet, gain 0.025).
  Voice gain 1.6 before final normalise. Final: loudnorm I=-14 LUFS, TP -1.5, AAC 160k.
  Decided against (16 Nov): background music (all 5 options + guzheng tested) -> replaced
  by kopitiam chatter; synthetic slurp/ahh (too rough); synthetic café sounds.
  Music options kept on file if ever needed: lo-fi kafe, guzheng, dokumentari, piano tenang.


8. CONTENT AND LEGAL RULES
--------------------------
  - Allegations: always "didakwa"/"disyaki", and include the other side's denial.
    Only state as fact what is on record (e.g. resignation via Nvidia 8-K).
  - Show "Sumber: ..." on screen for every news fact and figure.
  - No real people's faces or photos, no company logos, no flags of real brands.
    Silhouettes, icons, AI footage of anonymous/blurred people only.
  - Titles: factual. A question mark only if the event has not happened.
  - AI disclosure: switch ON the AI-generated content label on TikTok/YouTube/Instagram
    (AI voice + AI footage).
  - Book cover: never show an AI-generated cover as the real one. Use a photo of the real
    book, or text only (current closing uses text).
  - Affiliate disclosure goes in the caption/bio ("link affiliate").
  - POLITICAL / ELECTION / ISSUE-BASED topics on TikTok: TikTok bans political content in branded or
    commercial posts (17 Nov 2026: episode 2 was removed for this). For these episodes post a
    separate TikTok version made with  make_episode.py render <ep> --no-book  (voice cut before
    the book line, closing card "Ikut kami @kafe.lembaran"), caption WITHOUT the book or affiliate
    wording, commercial content toggle OFF. YouTube and Instagram keep the normal version with the
    book. Non-political topics may use the book version on TikTok with the commercial toggle ON.


9. FILES AND HOW TO RENDER (pilot, hand-tuned)
----------------------------------------------
  SUPERSEDED by section 11. These scripts now live in video/legacy/ for reference.
  Repo folder video/ holds everything needed (copied from the work area):
    video/render_samples.py   base helpers: fonts F(), themes, make_bg, caption, banner/logo
    video/intro_template.py   opening: python3 intro_template.py "Line 1" "Line 2" [out.mp4]
    video/outro_template.py   closing: python3 outro_template.py "BOOK" "Author" "MM:SS:CC" [out.mp4]
    video/cards.py            visual panels (footage reader + infographics) - section 6
    video/render_vo3.py       full episode renderer (voice-synced). Edit at the top:
                              VO, VO_LEN, SCN_T, OUT_T, SUBS, SUB_END, BEATS, CARD (in cards.py),
                              titles in the intro/outro calls, output name.
    video/assets/             banner.png, logo300.png, sil_*.png
    video/sfx/                shout.wav, ahh_A.wav, ting_B.wav, chatter_1.wav, chatter_2.wav
  Scripts expect the work layout /home/claude/samples (scripts + assets),
  /home/claude/gem (footage v1..v4.mp4, c1_ahhA.wav, c2_clinkA.wav),
  /home/claude/gem2 (c2.wav, c3.wav, shout.wav), /home/claude/vo (voice .wav),
  /home/claude/fonts (Montserrat, Inter, Anton, ShareTechMono, Oswald, Playfair,
  JetBrainsMono from github.com/google/fonts; Lora + Poppins are system fonts).
  Restore in a new session:
    mkdir -p /home/claude/samples /home/claude/gem /home/claude/gem2 /home/claude/vo
    cp video/*.py video/assets/* /home/claude/samples/
    cp video/sfx/ahh_A.wav /home/claude/gem/c1_ahhA.wav; cp video/sfx/ting_B.wav /home/claude/gem/c2_clinkA.wav
    cp video/sfx/chatter_1.wav /home/claude/gem2/c2.wav; cp video/sfx/chatter_2.wav /home/claude/gem2/c3.wav
    cp video/sfx/shout.wav /home/claude/gem2/shout.wav
    (footage clips are per episode: put them in /home/claude/gem as v1.mp4 ...)
  Render: cd /home/claude/samples && python3 render_vo3.py   (~2 min for 80 s)
  Pause timing: ffmpeg -i voice.wav -af silencedetect=noise=-40dB:d=0.18 -f null -
  Check: grab frames (ffmpeg -ss T -frames:v 1), make a contact sheet, look at it.
  Network: workspace cannot reach Pexels/Unsplash/Pixabay/TTS/Hugging Face; all audio and
  footage come from the user (Gemini / AI Studio / phone recordings).


10. POSTING
-----------
  Copy the final .mp4 into media/ in this repo, commit, push -> GitHub Pages serves it at
  https://kafelembaran.github.io/kafelembaran.com/media/<file>.mp4
  Search metadata (every post): caption starts with the searchable topic words people type
  ("PRN Melaka 2026: ..."); names of people, parties and places in the caption text; 10-15 hashtags
  (topic, year, parties/people, then #duahirupankopi #kafelembaran #bukumalaysia), no #fyp spam;
  YouTube title starts with the topic, 12-16 YouTube tags incl. the teaching hook (e.g. "pagoda Toji");
  TikTok title = short topic line; category NEWS_POLITICS or EDUCATION; TikTok "third-party commercial
  content" ON because of the affiliate link; AI labels ON.
  Metricool (connector): createScheduledPost with the public URL; TikTok privacy and
  YouTube type "short"; set isAigc / isAiGeneratedContent = true. First post private,
  check, then public.


11. AUTOMATIC PIPELINE (from 16 Nov 2026)
-----------------------------------------
  One folder per episode:  episodes/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>/
      episode.json        the whole episode as data (see the pilot for a full example)
      voice.wav           from AI Studio (not committed)
      clips/*.mp4         Gemini footage, optional (not committed; missing clip -> text panel)
      tts_script.txt      generated: what the user pastes into AI Studio
      gemini_prompts.txt  generated: footage prompts for the user
      out/<slug>.mp4      generated video + out/sheet.png (one frame per scene for checking)

  Kit (video/):  kl.py (theme, fonts, opening + closing cards), panels.py (all panel types),
                 make_episode.py (commands below), fonts/, assets/, sfx/.
      python3 video/make_episode.py script episodes/<ep>   -> tts_script.txt + gemini_prompts.txt
      python3 video/make_episode.py align  episodes/<ep>   -> sentence timings found in voice.wav
      python3 video/make_episode.py render episodes/<ep>   -> out/<slug>.mp4 + out/sheet.png (~1.5 min)
  Alignment is automatic: pauses are found with silencedetect (-34 dB, 0.12 s), then dynamic
  programming splits the speech into the script's sentences by their spoken SYLLABLE count (acronyms
  by letter: MCA = 3, UMNO = 2; digits as words), preferring long pauses. Check: the speaking rate per
  sentence should come out even (about 5-7 syllables a second for Enzo). Tested on the pilot:
  identical to the hand timing. If a sentence lands wrong, check with "align" and adjust the
  script (each sentence must be read in order, no extra words).

  episode.json fields:
    slug, date, title [line1, line2], book {title, author, shopee},
    intro_say (fixed hook), outro_say ("Nak faham ... Baca <Buku>. Link kat bio."),
    scenes[]: head {kind: big|type|count|stamp, text | value+prefix+suffix, sub},
              panel {type: clip|cores|pair|calendar|timeline|equals|block|chain|middle|bars|text, ...}
                    (clip: file, start, prompt, fallback, optional bar {label, value}),
              source (shown as "Sumber: ..."),
              say[]: sentences; string, or {"say": spoken words, "show": subtitle text with *gold*}.
    post {caption, hashtags, youtube_title, youtube_tags, category}, sources [urls].
  Panel parameters are listed at the top of video/panels.py.

  WHO DOES WHAT
    Schedule: no fixed days. A daily check (12:05pm) keeps at least 2 episodes a week and never more
    than 1 waiting for the user's voice. An episode counts as published when media/<slug>.mp4 exists
    (so always name the published video exactly after the episode slug).
    Claude (scheduled check):  scan news -> choose 1 issue + matching book -> research with
        sources -> write episode.json (10-12 scenes, rules in section 8) -> run "script" ->
        commit -> send the user: topic summary, tts_script.txt, gemini_prompts.txt.
    User (~5 min):  approve/adjust the topic, generate voice in AI Studio (Enzo, Friendly),
        optionally the Gemini clips, send them back in the chat.
    Claude (in chat):  put files in the episode folder -> render -> check sheet.png and the
        alignment -> send the video -> on approval: copy to media/, push, schedule private on
        TikTok + YouTube via Metricool (AI label on) -> user checks -> public + Instagram Reel.


12. DESIGN RULES: ANTI-SLOP (from 17 Nov 2026, applies from the next episode)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Every episode is designed with the "frontend-design" skill (anti-slop design). Load it with the
  Skill tool before choosing panels, headline wording or any visual change, and follow it.
  Audit of the pilot against the skill's list of generic "AI-made" tells (all to be removed):
   - ALL-CAPS labels ("DUA HIRUPAN KOPI", "BUKU DALAM VIDEO INI", "LINK BUKU KAT BIO")
   - middle-dot strings ("TikTok · YouTube · Instagram", "Anggaran · Fortune")
   - monospace clock for a small data label
   - every panel in the same rounded box with the same gold border (SaaS-card kit)
   - single word picked out in gold (subtitle *didakwa*, gold second title line)
   - the same fade-and-slide-up on every element
   - big centred number + small label as the default for every headline

  Design direction v2 "MEJA KOPITIAM" (mock: video/design/meja-kopitiam-mock.png,
  code: video/design/meja_kopitiam_mock.py). The video happens on a kopitiam table:
   Colour   brand green #165450 (wall tiles, faint tile grid) | marble #ECE8E1 with soft grey veins
            (the table: holds footage and diagrams) | order-slip yellow #F3E6B5 with blue ruled
            lines and a red margin line | menu-board red #B8322B (numbers, stamps; sparingly) |
            kopi brown #3B2618 (writing on the slip) | cream #F7F1E8 (text on green).
   Type     Anton (painted menu-board lettering) for numbers and headlines; Inter for subtitles,
            sources and small text; Lora only in the logo/banner and the hook quote.
   Layout   left-aligned. Headline written on an order slip (auto-sized to its text, tilted
            -3..+3 degrees, torn bottom edge, soft shadow) top-left. Footage/diagram sits on the
            marble table, no border box. Kopitiam wall clock (analog dial + Anton time + "antara dua
            hirupan kopi") top-left. Subtitles left-aligned, Inter Bold, on a dark band above the
            banner. Source in kopi brown at the bottom-right of the marble.
   Motion   ONE moment per scene: the slip slaps down onto the table (drop + small bounce). Cuts
            between scenes. No fade-up on every element.
   Words    sentence case everywhere ("Link buku kat bio", "Baca buku ini"); lists written as
            words ("di TikTok, YouTube dan Instagram"); no single highlighted word; no eyebrow labels.
   Boldness is spent only on the slip; everything else stays quiet.
  Checklist before sending any render: look at sheet.png and confirm no text overflows a slip,
  no caps labels, no middle dots, one motion per scene, subtitles readable, sources readable.
  Status: BUILT (17 Nov 2026) as video/style_kopitiam.py. An episode uses it with "style": "kopitiam"
  in episode.json (the pilot keeps the old look). New panels: pagoda (swaying floors, central pillar,
  floor labels, pillar label, height label, question mark), flex (rigid cracks vs flexible sways),
  seats (seat dots by party), seatrows (one row of seats per election), trio (three people holding a
  pillar), versus (two columns, optional tick or cross). bars takes "highlight": index.


